				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Yup it's true about grandmastery....Only can choose one.  I am not sure what that is going to be for myself.  The 'easiest' not that any are easy after you get to like 100... would probably be pottery.  And there are some purty nifty things you can make with a higher pottery skill.  Idols of tunare etc....So that has been my train of thought, but I do need to read more on the Xanthe and solstice quest so I can think of what might be the best one for both quest's to master.  And yup Elanae can have both earrings  <img src="images/smiles/icon_biggrin.gif" alt="icon_biggrin.gif" border="0" /> I plan on getting all tradeskills as close to 200 as I can...
<br />

<br />
And Q as far as Shawl 3 goes, it's a lot of time in Eastern wastes.  We need 1 Tundra kodiak meat, 2 snow bunny meat(which they are like level 5 mobs that will be easy enough, if you can see them through the snow), 2 ulthork meat (which I scored some froma  vendor, so keep an eye peeled), and 4 snow griffon eggs(I believe these are no drop).  The monsters are easy enough to tackle. It's just doing it. I believe 3/4 of the meats are droppable, so I am keeping my eyes open for the meats.  but I am not holding my breath to finding much.  I've spent 0 time in Eastern Wastes, so I don't know the zone at all. That's been a major stumbling block for I am not one for exploring an unknown zone without someone as a guide, and my usual guide has been off EQ due to his wife just having a baby girl.   <img src="images/smiles/icon_smile.gif" alt="icon_smile.gif" border="0" />  So perhaps a venture to EW would not be a bad idea for a bunch of people.  BTW Q, I can log into forums now, but Lant and I still are not being able to use chat. 
<br />

<br />
Aria <img src="images/smiles/new_angel.gif" alt="new_angel.gif" border="0" /></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
